From ddb24ec7e1337688cbd9d0f557629d5effb8263e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AERA | Erez Yaary <yaary@me.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:11:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] ui: fsel_settle after the file selector; dlg_win_button,
 a window's button on release

EConvert's first (5 Nov 2026), the hub's yes to common. Erez: "when
selecting a file to convert, and then selecting the target, it forgets
the file and says there are 0 files to convert". A window whose buttons
act on a press can be given a click the file selector left as it
closed on a double click's first: EConvert's Clear.

fsel_settle (ui/fsel.c, new): after fsel_exinput, the button waited up
(2,000 polls at most) and the button events queued taken off (16 at
most). dlg_win_button (dialog.c): a press on a window's own EXIT button
taken as a dialog's are, only when let go over it (graf_watchbox): 0
for the button already up, let go elsewhere, disabled, not EXIT.

tests/dialog: five dlg_win_button checks (stand-in graf_mkstate and
graf_watchbox), 143 checks ok, both builds. tests/uibits (new, also
scr_work_size and enlarge_mark's): fsel_settle's three.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SZeNoDLt48EM4msuao4J1n
